id: pm-ekf2gu
title: item mutate --dry-run does not surface per-row advisory duplicate-detection warnings
description: "Bulk create rows run the full SDK create path, so governance.duplicate_detection_mode applies per row: strict refuses and advisory records a warning. The staged preview behind pm item mutate --dry-run returns validation metadata (validated, state, unresolved_commit_constraints) plus mutation_count, mutations, references, and rows, but none of those carry the per-row advisory warnings that create produced, so an agent importing a document under advisory mode cannot see which rows look like existing items before committing. Surface the advisory similarity warnings in the dry-run receipt, keyed by row index and ref, without changing the configured policy."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 3
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-15T19:59:23.318Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-19T11:10:19.163Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-19T11:05:50.779Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-19T11:05:50.779Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: Dry-run receipt lists each advisory similarity warning with the row index and ref; Strict mode still refuses the same rows and the configured policy is not changed; Receipt shape is covered by a unit test on the planner and an integration test on pm item mutate --dry-run
parent: pm-doxj
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "Collect original create lifecycle warnings during disposable preview and project them by source index and ref through one public SDK helper shared by CLI and MCP. Clear stale row warnings and preserve strict/off policy, replay semantics, and source bytes."
expected_result: "Advisory duplicate warnings identify affected rows before commit; strict policy still refuses, off policy omits warnings, and preview leaves durable source state unchanged."
actual_result: Hosted CI39239473255 passes complete exact 100/100/100/100 coverage and all platform/runtime/package gates at51746b997835959d86847d1eb8f6c1287e78738f. Linked53 tests pass; the explicit MCP-response guard rerun also passes53 and all four TypeScript projects. Actual tarball SDK consumers pass under Node and Bun; npx/bunx packaged acceptance and complete static quality pass. Final analyzer/reviewer revalidation remains required on PR1506 before merge.
