comments[10]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T08:40:03.919Z","harness:codex","Selected with pm-fa9olc for one SDK-first actionable-preview delivery. Full strict all-status intake covers 3000 records, 2724 closed, no omissions/unreadables and no existing in-progress ownership. Existing shipped preview-safety owners were read live and remain completed. Implement shared staged warning receipts with per-row index/ref, preserve duplicate policy and no-write behavior, verify SDK plus CLI/MCP transport. GitHub intake: no open PRs or security alerts; every open issue already has a canonical PM link comment."
  "2026-10-19T08:51:09.876Z","harness:codex","Failed-before evidence: keeper SDK tests on unchanged production omitted advisory warning receipts; off mode also lacked the declared empty collection. Existing strict duplicate refusal was independently confirmed at conflict exit4 (the initial test expectation of usage exit2 was corrected, without changing policy). Final focused suite passes149 tests across six files, including actual CLI/MCP source-row ref parity and immutable durable snapshots. Shared SDK preview collects original lifecycle create warnings and public previewItemMutationDocument joins them to source rows without changing the input plan; replay remains explicitly unvalidated with no fresh warnings. Conservative SDK signature gate acknowledges the additive result/row/context contracts and the new public projection helper."
  "2026-10-19T09:17:23.167Z","harness:codex","Complete local coverage attempt finished10771 passed/6 failed/3 platform skips; it is a failed attempt, not coverage proof. One packed continuation fixture reports missing global npm/package.json under this Homebrew Node layout and explicitly prescribes NODE_PATH; five existing controls timed out under parallel load (merge portability, canonical examples, refusal closure, two surface-replication cases). Retain all failures. Retry the exact failed files with the advertised environment recovery and bounded workers, unchanged source/assertions/deadlines, then rerun complete coverage. New preview controls remain green."
  "2026-10-19T09:24:32.872Z","harness:codex","The unchanged failed-file retry passes40/40 tests with the advertised NODE_PATH recovery and two workers; no time ceiling or assertion changed. Pre-PR projection review also found a new-helper edge case: a caller reusing rows from a prior preview could retain stale warnings after policy changes. The keeper fails before the correction and now rebuilds row warnings solely from the current staged receipt while preserving its input. Full coverage will be rerun on this corrected source."
  "2026-10-19T10:03:49.557Z","harness:codex","Upstream changelog compatibility is now delivered: PR256 restores explicit full-list projection, and PR259 fixes the real npm numeric-suffix mandatory-tag refusal with explicit latest. Corrective release2026.10.19-1 completed workflow39233360234; independent exact/latest registry integrity matches, GitHub release points to d80fdea89c7b84d0dafb4a17b156db0eadcff6e7, and hosted Bun installation passes. Use the latest published package for this branch's generated changelog. No root same-day auto-release is created."
  "2026-10-19T10:40:19.939Z","harness:codex","Local delivery gates pass: complete static quality including lint, generated contracts, SDK surface, package boundaries, behavior/cost gates and mutation assurance; all four TypeScript projects; version synchronization; tracked credential scan; and zero-vulnerability dependency audit. The linked warning command executes53 passing tests with local trust and isolated schema roots. Final complete exact-count coverage remains a required hosted gate before review closeout."
  "2026-10-19T10:42:51.998Z","harness:codex","Packaged npx acceptance passes using the staged publication artifact: executable aliases, isolated workflow, installed consumer types and package capabilities. The latest pm-changelog2026.10.19-1 generator and canonical check both pass. Preparing one PR for the two SDK preview items and their unchanged-deadline verification cohort; keep claims active for complete hosted coverage and review, then land structured closure evidence and regenerate the changelog on that same PR."
  "2026-10-19T10:45:42.649Z","harness:codex","Review delivery: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1506 at implementation head51746b997835959d86847d1eb8f6c1287e78738f. One consolidated configured-bot request is posted with all three canonical PM links. Complete hosted coverage and exact-head review are running; final closure evidence will be committed on this same PR after the result."
  "2026-10-19T11:04:33.037Z","harness:codex","First hosted CI39239473255 succeeds, including complete coverage and all platform/runtime/package gates. External DeepScan reports one NULL_POINTER in the new semantic-preview test at its optional MCP response cast (https://deepscan.io/dashboard/#view=project&pid=32092&iid=237823220). Chrome inspection confirms the exact source. Add an explicit structured-content guard before casting the test receipt; no product behavior changes. CodeRabbit's only actionable finding concerns exact dependency timestamps and is corrected through the PM CLI, preserving immutable history. Final head will retrigger every configured reviewer and all required checks."
  "2026-10-19T11:10:19.163Z","harness:codex","Closeout assurance: all three live full item/history reads confirm closed status, released ownership, and resolution/expected/actual/reason fields together in each immutable close event. Defect evidence and recurrence gates pass. Full tracker history validation checks3001 items with zero missing/unreadable streams, hash/chain mismatches, version skew or workspace drift. Validation retains170 historical resolution-metadata advisories, and health exits0 with14 advisory warnings; these are not claimed repaired by the preview delivery. The package-generated changelog includes all three completed items under Unreleased."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T08:54:32.466Z","harness:codex",A staged mutation preview must carry the lifecycle advisories it evaluated alongside its validation verdict. Join advisories by source row position and alias in the SDK so transports cannot disagree; a committed-plan replay must remain distinguishable from a fresh policy evaluation.
